I was playing a weaponless monk whose quiver consisted of a dwarvish
mattock when this thought popped into my head:

Hitting with a thrown a thrown two-handed or heavy weapon with a
strength of 18 or higher sometimes results in an increase damage bonus
(d(weight/10)) and you doubly exercise your strength and dexterity:
("<monster> staggers from the force of impact")

Throwing a two-handed or heavy weapon (regardless of strength or
dexterity) will sometimes go horribly wrong:  ("You throw wildly off
target.")  The weapon then goes flying off in a random direction, and
may still hit something.  "<weapon> ricochets off the <ceiling || wall>
and hits <monster || you>"  If it hits you, the weapon does double
damage.  If it hits a monster, the weapon does normal damage.
Regardless, you take d(25-constitution) damage and doubly abuse your
strength and dexterity ("You pull something.")

